[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: StrictDoc tooling for this repository

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: grammar.sgra

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE
TITLE: Store the parent contract fingerprint in the node
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A second consumer needs per-edge state that a node field cannot carry, such as
a reviewer identity or a waiver with its own expiry.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
A node records the contract hash of each parent it depends on, in a PARENT_FP
field on the node itself, rather than in a sidecar file keyed by node identity.
Fingerprints point strictly downward: DECISION to MECHANISM to SLICE.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Accepting a change becomes a reviewable git diff, attributable to a commit and
revertable. A sidecar makes sign-off invisible and needs a key-matching scheme.
The downward-only rule means a garbage-collectable node has no inbound
fingerprint, so deleting it can never strand one.
<<<

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-LOCAL-IMPLEMENTABILITY
TITLE: Implementability is a property of a closure, not of the project
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A release needs a single project-wide readiness answer, which no per-slice
query can supply.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
A slice is implementable when its own transitive contract-dependency closure is
settled and carries no suspect edges. There is no global readiness gate. The
count of open decisions in that closure is the slice's degrees of freedom, and
handoff is that count reaching zero.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A global fail-closed gate is waterfall by construction: nothing is implementable
until everything is designed. A closure-local predicate lets a mature slice ship
while the rest of the graph stays deliberately fuzzy.
<<<

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-DEFER-LAYER
TITLE: Omit the LAYER node type until a corpus with layers arrives
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: >>>
The first document whose mechanisms sit in distinct architectural layers, at
which point the cast tables' locus column becomes the LAYER assignment.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The grammar ships without LAYER. Horizontal position is therefore unmodelled;
only the vertical axis, a SLICE and the mechanisms it Crosses, is expressible.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No content in this document sits in a layer. Adding LAYER now would make every
MECHANISM carry a field with one possible value.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
This is a real gap, not a cost-free deferral: half the horizontal-and-vertical
tracking the operator asked for is absent until it is closed.
<<<

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-FP-CHECK
TITLE: Suspect-link detection over the JSON export
DEPTH: needs-spike
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Hash each node's contract-bearing fields from the JSON export. A node is suspect
when a parent it records a fingerprint for no longer hashes to the recorded
value, or when that parent has been deleted. Excludes RATIONALE and NOTES.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
StrictDoc has no suspect-link feature. It is on the upstream backlog as
SDOC-SRS-117 and described unbuilt in their DO-178 notes.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE:0000000
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE
  ROLE: Governed_By

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-CYCLE-CHECK
TITLE: Cycle detection over the JSON export
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Detect relation cycles in the exported graph independently of StrictDoc.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
StrictDoc's own cycle detection queries the graph without specifying an edge
role, and the graph database returns only the bucket of role-less edges. Every
relation in this grammar carries a role, so no cycle in this corpus is detected;
the failure surfaces as a recursion-depth crash during render.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-LOCAL-IMPLEMENTABILITY:0000000
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-LOCAL-IMPLEMENTABILITY
  ROLE: Governed_By

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-READY-QUERY
TITLE: Ready-slice query over the contract closure
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Walk a slice's contract-dependency closure and report whether every mechanism in
it is interface-settled or better, every decision accepted, and no edge suspect.
Report the blocking frontier and the open-decision count otherwise. The same
traversal produces the bounded prompt handed to an implementing model.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-LOCAL-IMPLEMENTABILITY:0000000
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-LOCAL-IMPLEMENTABILITY
  ROLE: Governed_By

[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-SEMBLE-SDOC
TITLE: Index sdoc documents in semble via a tree-sitter grammar
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Package a tree-sitter grammar for the sdoc format as a flake output and register
it with semble, so sdoc documents are chunked on node boundaries rather than by
line count.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The semble integration already accepts arbitrary tree-sitter grammar packages.
This slice crosses no mechanism in this document and has zero open decisions in
its closure.
<<<

[SPIKE]
UID: SPIKE-SGRA-PARSE
TITLE: Make the tree-sitter grammar parse standalone .sgra files
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: unrun
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A three-rule patch is applied and the two .sgra files parse with no regression
across the sdoc corpus.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The upstream tree-sitter grammar parses all sdoc documents but fails every
standalone .sgra grammar file, because its root rule requires a DOCUMENT header.
<<<
